# ── PROD CHECKLIST ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Before any non-local deploy:
#   1. Set every *_CORS below to the REAL origins (these are localhost/VPN-only).
#   2. JWT_SECRET / COOKIE_SECRET must be long random values, never defaults —
#      generate each with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
#      (rotating them logs every admin + customer out; that is expected).
#   3. Run with NODE_ENV=production so the storefront's _polycards_jwt cookie is
#      marked Secure (and serve over HTTPS, or the cookie will be dropped).
#      (medusa-config.ts also REFUSES to boot in production on missing/default
#      secrets.)
#   4. req.ip / per-IP rate limiting: Medusa HARDCODES Express "trust proxy"
#      to 1 (@medusajs/framework express-loader, no config knob). That is
#      correct behind EXACTLY ONE proxy/LB. Two failure modes to check:
#      - Exposed DIRECTLY (no proxy): clients can spoof X-Forwarded-For and
#        rotate req.ip per request, bypassing the per-IP auth limiter — put a
#        proxy in front, or override the setting (one-time
#        req.app.set("trust proxy", false) in a global middleware).
#      - TWO OR MORE hops (CDN + LB): req.ip resolves to the next proxy's IP
#        (e.g. the CDN edge), so clients collapse onto a handful of proxy IPs
#        sharing limiter budgets — override to the real hop count.
#      Either way: verify req.ip resolves to the actual client IP at deploy.
#   5. ALLOW_MOCK_TOPUP must stay UNSET in production. Unset keeps the mock
#      credit gateway OFF; topup.ts fails closed and refuses ALLOW_MOCK_TOPUP=true
#      under NODE_ENV=production. Wire a real payment provider before deploy
#      (see the Feature gates section below).
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
STORE_CORS=http://localhost:8000,https://docs.medusajs.com
ADMIN_CORS=http://localhost:7000,http://localhost:9000
VENDOR_CORS=http://localhost:7001
AUTH_CORS=http://localhost:7000,http://localhost:7001,http://localhost:9000
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
JWT_SECRET=supersecret
COOKIE_SECRET=supersecret
DATABASE_URL=
# Public origin of the Next.js storefront — used to build the password-reset
# link emailed (currently: logged) to customers. No trailing slash.
STOREFRONT_URL=http://localhost:4000

# ── Image storage (POST /admin/media) ───────────────────────────────────────
# UNSET → Medusa's built-in LOCAL provider (writes to static/; fine for dev,
# lost on redeploy). Set ALL of S3_BUCKET + S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID +
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY to switch medusa-config.ts to the S3 provider (durable
# object storage + CDN). Works with AWS S3 or any S3-compatible store (R2,
# MinIO, Backblaze). The route stores the ORIGINAL image untouched; the
# storefront derives display sizes with next/image.
# S3_BUCKET=
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# S3_REGION=auto                                  # R2: "auto"
# S3_ENDPOINT=                                    # R2: https://<account>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# S3_FILE_URL=                                    # public base URL files are served from (CDN/bucket public URL)

# Instant ("sell on the spot") buyback window after a pull, in ms (default 90000 =
# the 30s on-reveal keep/sell countdown plus animation/network grace). Inside the
# window the pack's buyback_percent applies; after it, the flat rate (90).
# BUYBACK_INSTANT_WINDOW_MS=90000

# Rate limits (burst + sustained sliding windows; Redis-backed via REDIS_URL with
# in-memory failover). Defaults in src/api/utils/rate-limit.ts; all optional.
# Pack opens, per customer (default 5/10s + 20/60s):
# PACK_OPEN_RATE_BURST_LIMIT= / PACK_OPEN_RATE_BURST_WINDOW_MS= / PACK_OPEN_RATE_LIMIT= / PACK_OPEN_RATE_WINDOW_MS=
# Buybacks, per customer (default 10/10s + 30/60s):
# VAULT_BUYBACK_RATE_BURST_LIMIT= / VAULT_BUYBACK_RATE_BURST_WINDOW_MS= / VAULT_BUYBACK_RATE_LIMIT= / VAULT_BUYBACK_RATE_WINDOW_MS=
# Auth credential endpoints (login/register/password reset), per IP (default 5/10s + 20/60s):
# AUTH_RATE_BURST_LIMIT= / AUTH_RATE_BURST_WINDOW_MS= / AUTH_RATE_LIMIT= / AUTH_RATE_WINDOW_MS=
# Vault/credits reads, per customer (default 30/10s + 120/60s):
# STORE_READ_RATE_BURST_LIMIT= / STORE_READ_RATE_BURST_WINDOW_MS= / STORE_READ_RATE_LIMIT= / STORE_READ_RATE_WINDOW_MS=
# Credit top-ups (mock gateway), per customer (default 5/10s + 15/60s):
# CREDIT_TOPUP_RATE_BURST_LIMIT= / CREDIT_TOPUP_RATE_BURST_WINDOW_MS= / CREDIT_TOPUP_RATE_LIMIT= / CREDIT_TOPUP_RATE_WINDOW_MS=

# PriceCharting Prices API token (paid subscription; the 	 query param). Server-side only, never commit a real value.
PRICECHARTING_API_TOKEN=
# PriceCharting user id — REQUIRED by Inventory > "Add from PC Collection".
# The API token only AUTHENTICATES; it does not scope /api/offers to your
# account, so without this the API answers with every user's offers instead of
# your collection (and the page refuses to run rather than import strangers'
# cards). Your 26-character code is in the URL of your
# pricecharting.com/selling-available page. Not a secret.
PRICECHARTING_SELLER_ID=
# Optional override for the USD->MYR FX feed (defaults to Frankfurter).
FX_USD_MYR_URL=

# ── Feature gates ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rewards economy (daily draw / claim / withdraw). Dormant unless set to the
# exact string "true"; unset keeps every rewards route a no-op (rewards-gate.ts).
# REWARDS_REDEMPTION_ENABLED=
# Vendor commission cooldown, in days. Overrides the built-in default; 0 makes
# commissions instant (demo/seed use). Unset -> default cooldown (packs service).
# Mock credit-topup gateway opt-in. Unset -> OFF. "true" enables it (rejected in
# production by topup.ts); "unsafe-demo" forces it on for a deliberate demo
# deploy. MUST stay unset in prod (see PROD CHECKLIST item 5 above).
# ALLOW_MOCK_TOPUP=

# ── Payouts (withdrawal approval, daily cap, destination cooldown) ──────────
# Withdrawals above this RM figure are written 'held' — debited but never sent
# to the gateway — until an admin approves/denies from the admin /withdrawals
# queue (default view: held). Strictly greater-than: RM 1,000.00 exactly still
# auto-submits. Unset -> default 1000. Read per call, never latched at boot.
# Setting this to 0 does NOT hold every payout today — it falls back to the
# default (0 holds every payout from plan 095 onward).
# GLOBEPAY_WD_APPROVAL_ABOVE_RM=1000
# Rolling-24h cap on one customer's summed withdrawals, in RM. Unset -> default
# 50000. Unlike the threshold above, 0 IS meaningful here and on purpose: the
# operator's stop-lever for money-out during an incident. Read per call.
# GLOBEPAY_WD_DAILY_MAX_RM=50000
# Cooling-off window, in hours, between saving a new payout destination (bank
# account) and being allowed to pay out to it — the control on the
# steal-a-token -> add-a-destination -> cash-out chain. Unset -> default 24.
# 0 is a deliberate, explicit operator opt-out (never a fallback: a fraction,
# a negative, or garbage input all still resolve to 24 and warn).
# PAYOUT_DESTINATION_COOLDOWN_HOURS=24

# ── GlobePay callback + return URLs (REQUIRED — all four fail closed) ────────
# Absolute https URLs on the deployed backend/storefront. None has a default and
# no error message names the missing variable, so provisioning from this template
# without them yields a silently dead money channel.
# The FIRST pair below opens the top-up channel: unset, POST /store/credits/deposit
# refuses every top-up with "Top-ups are temporarily unavailable."
# The SECOND pair opens the payout channel, and gates TWO routes: unset, the
# customer withdrawal route refuses with "Withdrawals are not open yet." and the
# admin held-withdrawal approval refuses with "The payout channel is closed".
# Failing closed is deliberate, not a bug: without a reachable notify endpoint a
# customer could pay and never be credited, and a failed payout could never
# refund itself. Live values live in .do/backend.app.yaml (and the DO app secrets);
# docs/payments/globepay365-setup.md documents what each endpoint must serve.
# GLOBEPAY_NOTIFY_URL=
# GLOBEPAY_RETURN_URL=
# GLOBEPAY_WITHDRAW_NOTIFY_URL=
# GLOBEPAY_PAYOUT_VERIFY_URL=

# ── TGPay (alternative gateway, plan 130) ───────────────────────────────────
# PAYMENT_GATEWAY selects the HTTP client behind the same deposit/withdrawal
# machinery: unset or `globepay` keeps GlobePay365; `tgpay` uses TGPay. The
# GLOBEPAY_ENABLED / GLOBEPAY_WITHDRAWALS_ENABLED switches and the four URL
# vars above still apply — point the two NOTIFY URLs at /hooks/tgpay/deposit
# and /hooks/tgpay/withdrawal (TGPay has no payout-verify step, so
# GLOBEPAY_PAYOUT_VERIFY_URL is ignored for it). An explicit NOTIFY URL only
# counts for a gateway when it ends in that gateway's hook path.
# Keys: TGPay admin → Platform → Settings → General (the secret needs 2FA on).
# docs/payments/tgpay-setup.md has the sandbox walkthrough.
# PAYMENT_GATEWAY=tgpay
# TGPAY_API_BASE=https://sandbox-api.tgpay365.com/api/v2
# TGPAY_PUBLIC_KEY=
# TGPAY_SECRET_KEY=
# TGPAY_CURRENCY=MYR
# Only if their hosted checkout is not served from the API host minus "-api":
# TGPAY_CHECKOUT_BASE=https://sandbox.tgpay365.com
# Callback source allowlist (TGPay asked for one on top of the key headers).
# Comma/space-separated IPv4 addresses or CIDR blocks; when set, both TGPay
# hooks answer 403 to any other source, judged on the proxy-established
# address (req.ip), never on X-Forwarded-For. Unset = header-only, which is
# what the sandbox needs (it calls from addresses they did not list).
# Production list as given by TGPay on 2026-09-05:
# TGPAY_CALLBACK_IPS=1.32.102.191,1.32.102.19,60.48.120.36,219.95.78.237,1.32.102.35,219.94.46.237,1.32.102.1,18.142.49.112,188.114.96.0,188.114.97.0,47.131.132.118,54.251.58.7
# The ACTIVE gateway is an admin setting (Settlement page → Payment gateway),
# persisted on site_settings; PAYMENT_GATEWAY above is only the boot/fallback
# value. With PAYMENT_CALLBACK_BASE set (our public backend origin) the two
# NOTIFY URLs and the payout-verify URL are derived per gateway from its hook
# paths, so a switch needs no URL edits; unset, the explicit GLOBEPAY_*_URL
# values apply unchanged.
# PAYMENT_CALLBACK_BASE=https://api.example.com

# ── Phone verification (SMS OTP) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Destinations POST /store/phone-verification/start will text, comma-separated
# ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes. That route is UNAUTHENTICATED and every call bills a
# real SMS, so this is the geo-lock that bounds an SMS-pumping run. Unset, empty
# or whitespace -> the default set (MY) — never "everywhere", never "nowhere".
# Two things must move WITH any widening, or it half-lands:
#   1. the ISO->dialling-code row in src/utils/phone-verification.ts (an unlisted
#      code resolves to no prefix and therefore widens nothing), and
#   2. ALLOWED_PHONE_COUNTRIES in the storefront's src/lib/profile-validation.ts
#      (otherwise the picker offers a country whose code never arrives).
# Not a secret — a plain value in .do/backend.app.yaml.
# ALLOWED_SMS_COUNTRIES=MY

# ── Ops knobs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Medusa worker split: "shared" (dev / all-in-one), "server", or "worker". The
# platform sets this per component; local dev leaves it shared (medusa-config.ts).
# MEDUSA_WORKER_MODE=
# Public storefront origin the backend redirects /cdn/cards/* art to (falls back
# to a hardcoded prod URL when unset). No trailing slash.
# MERCUR_STOREFRONT_URL=
# Rolling-24h ceiling, in RM, on credit MINTED by manual admin adjustments.
# Counts POSITIVE `adjustment` rows only, summed GLOBALLY (every admin, every
# customer) over the trailing 24h; clawbacks (negative adjustments) never count
# and are never blocked. Default 1000000 — equal to the per-call ADJUST_MAX_RM,
# so one full-size grant per day passes and a second one is refused.
# This is the aggregate bound: the per-call ceiling plus the admin rate limiter
# alone would permit ~RM 200,000,000/min of minted credit, and minted credit
# banks zero playthrough (external_funded_cents = 0), i.e. it is immediately
# withdrawable. Set to 0 to refuse EVERY positive adjustment — the incident
# stop lever (0 is honoured, not treated as unset).
# ADJUST_DAILY_MINT_MAX_RM=1000000

# ── Admin provisioning (src/scripts/create-admin.ts) ─────────────────────────
# Super-admin bootstrapped idempotently on run. Email defaults when unset; if
# ADMIN_PASSWORD is unset the script skips admin creation.
# ADMIN_EMAIL=
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# --- Google OAuth (storefront customer social login) ---
# From the Google Cloud console OAuth client (Cloud project "polycards").
# All three are required for the `google` auth provider to register; if any is
# unset the backend boots with emailpass only (see medusa-config.ts auth module).
# CALLBACK_URL must exactly match an Authorised redirect URI on the OAuth client;
# the storefront overrides it per-request, but the provider still needs a default.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:3000/auth/google/callback

# --- Resend (transactional email: password reset) ---
# API_KEY + FROM_EMAIL are BOTH required to register the email provider; with either
# unset the backend boots with the local/feed notification provider only and password
# reset emails are skipped with a warn (see medusa-config.ts + modules/resend/options.ts).
# Leave unset for local dev: dev/test log the reset link to the console instead of
# sending, so a dev box never emits live mail even with real credentials present.
# FROM_EMAIL must be on a domain verified in Resend. Send from a SUBDOMAIN
# (send.polycards.gg) so its SPF/DKIM records stay clear of the root domain's
# Google Workspace mail records.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxx
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=Polycards <noreply@send.polycards.gg>
# Optional. Without it, customer replies to a transactional email go nowhere.
# RESEND_REPLY_TO=support@polycards.gg

# ── Telegram apex board (Legendary+ pulls → public channel) ──────────────
# All four optional: unset = feature off (dev/CI default). See
# src/modules/packs/telegram.ts header for full semantics.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Numeric channel id (e.g. -100…). Quote it in YAML specs — leading '-'.
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# Lowest posted tier. Default Legendary. NOTE: RARITY_ORDER puts Mythical
# BELOW Legendary — set 'Mythical' to WIDEN the board by one tier.
TELEGRAM_MIN_RARITY=
# Storefront origin for profile links. Default https://polycards.gg.
TELEGRAM_SITE_URL=
